{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/831580-must-a-scion-ascend","id":831580,"title":"Must a Scion ascend?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-17T01:12:29-08:00","id":831580,"title":"Must a Scion ascend?","content":"One of the things about 1e was that it pretty much encouraged you to go from Hero to Demigod to God. That was basically your whole path - become the next generation of gods. Even the powers where such that at Hero level your powers were, all things considered, not really that cool. <br /> <br /> Now I have not read any of the Percy Jackson books, only seen the movies. However, they don't seem to be in any rush to become gods, or even necessarily under the impression that they will become gods. Games based around the show Supernatural for its inspiration has no need to go to the Demigod or God level, it is pretty content to say at Hero. Similarly, a campaign based around the Thor movies as a concept has no need to start at Hero, easily starting at Demigod if not God level and staying there the whole time. <br /> <br /> Do we know enough yet to know if it would be possible to run a whole campaign at one threshold only?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Yes, yes, yes... I know it is a horror game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11143-feonorx","name":"Feonorx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T06:33:32-08:00","id":831702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Feonorx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/831580-must-a-scion-ascend#post831580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know enough yet to know if it would be possible to run a whole campaign at one threshold only?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2e, you should be able to. That's one of the design goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T17:34:02-08:00","id":832865,"title":"","content":"Well there are actually characters listed in the 1e books who have been Heroes / Demigods for centuries or even thousands of years.<br /> <br /> Circe and Ixion being two such examples.<br /> <br /> So it is possible, yes. But the question is &quot;why would they?&quot;<br /> <br /> The whole plot of Scion is that the Titans are free and laying siege to the gates of heaven and hell alike. The power of the Gods has waned since ancient times, which is why there has been an influx of Scions as of late. The Gods need reinforcements, and that's where you come in. You build up your power, establish connections, and then you join the gods and hit the front lines to stop the apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T20:40:46-08:00","id":832988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/831580-must-a-scion-ascend?p=832865#post832865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it is possible, yes. But the question is &quot;why would they?&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're looking at it from a player point of view. I can think of a bunch of examples of gods not ascending and for different reasons.<br /> <br /> Charon: has a job that doesn\u2019t really get him to the point of adventuring. So stuck in a rut due to profession/calling<br /> <br /> Magni/Modi/Thrud: Fate just plain old said so. You will survive Ragnarok and THEN become important. Till then enjoy your legend 10 and endless battles<br /> Ganymede: same as Charon<br /> <br /> The Graces: sure you\u2019re invited to everyone\u2019s party but you will always be in someone\u2019s retinue. Hell, you won\u2019t even be as big as a Muse\u2026but you get to come to all the parties.<br /> <br /> Momus: yer a dick. Get off my mountain. You don\u2019t get to hang out with any of the cool kids anymore so no one writes about you and no one cares about how you were mean spirited to some playwright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T21:15:12-08:00","id":833005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/831580-must-a-scion-ascend?p=832865#post832865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole plot of Scion is that the Titans are free and laying siege to the gates of heaven and hell alike. The power of the Gods has waned since ancient times, which is why there has been an influx of Scions as of late. The Gods need reinforcements, and that's where you come in. You build up your power, establish connections, and then you join the gods and hit the front lines to stop the apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole point of Scion's provided campaign, The Long Road to Heaven, is the Titan outbreak.<br /> <br /> But that's not expansive of its potential. Only one Scion campaign I've been a part of has followed that campaign, and almost none of the others have involved true Titans at all, let alone their actual escape from Tartarus.<br /> <br /> The point of scion is to play as mythical children of the gods, and ALL the legendary adventures that entails, not simply to fight the titans.<br /> <br /> So for the OP, I see no reason that a scion or Band would be uninterested in or even actively avoiding apotheosis. In fact, I can think of several reasons they'd be fine with their current lot in life and be uninterested in ascending to their parents' status.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10163-toomuchjesus","name":"Toomuchjesus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T21:57:34-08:00","id":833028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toomuchjesus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/831580-must-a-scion-ascend?p=833005#post833005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The point of scion is to play as mythical children of the gods, and ALL the legendary adventures that entails, not simply to fight the titans.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Had not considered that. Opens up a lot more options for story hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T10:32:41-08:00","id":833372,"title":"","content":"Many of the games I've run have had to do with inter-Pantheon tensions or conflict than dealing with the Titans. When the Titans have made an &quot;appearance&quot; it has been by proxy as &quot;3rd party&quot; by some supernatural agency which might be divine or just some organization of supernatural entities. <br /> <br /> One of the longest running Hero games consisted of a meta-plot of struggling with a band of Navajo Skinwalkers who were definitely doing things Titans would probably have liked and thought they were doing so on behalf of something that might or might not have been a Titan, but that was all muddled up at the end by finding out that they were actually cats-paws of a representative of a faction of Teotl. Or maybe they were working for the Titan really and he/it was too and didn't know it. Or something. The characters weren't really sure what they had accomplished other than defeating their enemies and stopping them from doing very very unpleasant things. Oh, and maybe, probably saved the world or at least a significant chunk of it (the part where they kept their stuff). <br /> <br /> In fact the most obvious direct Titan-related manifestation in that game was by an organization containing several corrupted Scions that kept telling the PCs to go away, because &quot;they weren't a part of THIS story&quot; and they needed to pay more attention to <i>their own</i> story... <br /> <br /> In others, the Titans were never an issue at all. Most pantheons contain creepy-crawlie enemy types that don't need to be working for some big bad beyond themselves. In fact, a lot of the various core deities can fill those roles to one degree or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T09:07:27-07:00","id":881030,"title":"","content":"remember VERY few Scions do ascend.. most die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T09:33:53-07:00","id":881044,"title":"","content":"Or most of them do... depending on how many Scions other than PCs are around. If the PCs are pretty much it, or a significant fraction of all the Scions around, and the PCs end up going for, ya know, the GOAL of the game, then it's a different situation altogether.... It all depends on the starting assumptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T23:57:40-07:00","id":881563,"title":"","content":"Imo &quot;not Ascending&quot; was always a possible mode of play. It was slightly hapered by fact singular tiers were not rich enough in features to properly sustain long campaign in them and this propostion being equivalent of Why would you want to play first 5 levels of DnD character only, when you can see all these goodies up ahead. Certainly possible, but not exactly that desirable by most for a long campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T08:57:25-07:00","id":881858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/831580-must-a-scion-ascend?p=881563#post881563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imo &quot;not Ascending&quot; was always a possible mode of play. It was slightly hapered by fact singular tiers were not rich enough in features to properly sustain long campaign in them and this propostion being equivalent of Why would you want to play first 5 levels of DnD character only, when you can see all these goodies up ahead. Certainly possible, but not exactly that desirable by most for a long campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, can say i agree on that at all, considering the sheer awesomeness that demigodhood per se can be - going God of War &amp; back and then some, with most of the group still around Legend 5-6 and having a hell of a time with it. Epics and Purviews up to 4-7 offer quite considerable power on their own, while still allowing the PCs to interact finely with the world and keeping some convenient power gap with their divine parents or the titan avatars (though that can be surprisingly debatable, as a demigod is perfectly capable of matching or even surpassing a deity in what are not their strong suites).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T16:23:38-07:00","id":882334,"title":"","content":"You could always just get the Extended Youth knack with Epic Stamina.<br /> <br /> Boom, immortality straight out of character creation!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T16:37:48-07:00","id":882340,"title":"","content":"If Memory serves, Extended Youth only makes you look younger. You still have the usual lifespan to be expected of a Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T17:09:45-07:00","id":882360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/831580-must-a-scion-ascend?p=882340#post882340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Memory serves, Extended Youth only makes you look younger. You still have the usual lifespan to be expected of a Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well that's going to be an awkward, spontaneous death by old age.<br /> <br /> Actually reading on it, it stops you from both visually<i> and physically aging. </i>So yeah, it is an early form of immortality.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#4E4F43\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At the physical age at which the character takes on this Knack, her body no longer physically or visibly ages. Her hair doesn\u2019t turn gray or thin out, her skin doesn\u2019t wrinkle, she doesn\u2019t get liver spots, nothing sags due to gravity. Until the character becomes a God, she looks like she looked at that mortal age.&quot;</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T16:05:25-07:00","id":884137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/831580-must-a-scion-ascend?p=882360#post882360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well that's going to be an awkward, spontaneous death by old age.<br /> <br /> Actually reading on it, it stops you from both visually<i> and physically aging. </i>So yeah, it is an early form of immortality.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#4E4F43\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At the physical age at which the character takes on this Knack, her body no longer physically or visibly ages. Her hair doesn\u2019t turn gray or thin out, her skin doesn\u2019t wrinkle, she doesn\u2019t get liver spots, nothing sags due to gravity. Until the character becomes a God, she looks like she looked at that mortal age.&quot;</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>So, basically an &quot;ageless, not immortal&quot; arrangement - that most PCs (&amp; NPCs) should be quite ok with overall, i guess. Truth be told, even most gods ain't immortal like that anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T17:56:58-07:00","id":884202,"title":"","content":"Meh, I consider eternal youth a form of immortality. True immortality as in being impossible to die would be a pretty crappy deal unless you had a mind capable of enduring it, which the Epic Intelligence might actually give you.<br /> <br /> But if your character can't actually <i>die</i> then it kind of takes the tension out of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T18:05:14-07:00","id":885052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/831580-must-a-scion-ascend?p=881563#post881563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imo &quot;not Ascending&quot; was always a possible mode of play. It was slightly hapered by fact singular tiers were not rich enough in features to properly sustain long campaign in them and this propostion being equivalent of Why would you want to play first 5 levels of DnD character only, when you can see all these goodies up ahead. Certainly possible, but not exactly that desirable by most for a long campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is, with D&amp;D 3.5 I've seen arguments for why you shouldn't go above level 6, generally similar arguments to how higher power level Scion games are generally broken.<br /> <br /> Now, I agree that ascending shouldn't be something required for a game, although I don't like the current system of 'free stuff when you reach Legend X' to represent moving across the tiers, I'd personally just remove the Demigod/God templates, give players relic-less purview access at Legend 5, and avoid any massive jumps in power.<br /> <br /> If I'm lucky I'll be running a Scion game starting in September/October, with the current plan for the campaign having no Titans in it (although the plan also currently doesn't cover anything above Legend 4), just a lot of scheming Scions and some escaped mythological creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T19:17:12-07:00","id":885086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/831580-must-a-scion-ascend?p=885052#post885052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The funny thing is, with D&amp;D 3.5 I've seen arguments for why you shouldn't go above level 6, generally similar arguments to how higher power level Scion games are generally broken.<br /> <br /> Now, I agree that ascending shouldn't be something required for a game, although I don't like the current system of 'free stuff when you reach Legend X' to represent moving across the tiers, I'd personally just remove the Demigod/God templates, give players relic-less purview access at Legend 5, and avoid any massive jumps in power.<br /> <br /> If I'm lucky I'll be running a Scion game starting in September/October, with the current plan for the campaign having no Titans in it (although the plan also currently doesn't cover anything above Legend 4), just a lot of scheming Scions and some escaped mythological creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yarr, that be your choice. But I bought Scion to feel like a super hero / villain, and lifting 6 million tons over my head with one finger (Making it Look Easy knack) is the kind of glorious power trip I adore in this setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-07-2016, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T02:06:17-07:00","id":885260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/831580-must-a-scion-ascend?p=885086#post885086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yarr, that be your choice. But I bought Scion to feel like a super hero / villain, and lifting 6 million tons over my head with one finger (Making it Look Easy knack) is the kind of glorious power trip I adore in this setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a case of I'm not sure what sort of players I'm going to have, so I'm waiting until I see them in action before planning the high powered stuff. Legend 4 is just what I thought would be a good place to pause planning where I could keep outlines fairly generic (Investigate here, beat up bad guy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:13:27-07:00","id":885416,"title":"","content":"one concern?<br /> <br /> considering the different power Tiers, and radically different themes, and such, should a ST Just Directly award Legend when neccessary, or what to make sure everyone ascends about the same time...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:27:00-07:00","id":885421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/831580-must-a-scion-ascend?p=885416#post885416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one concern?<br /> <br /> considering the different power Tiers, and radically different themes, and such, should a ST Just Directly award Legend when neccessary, or what to make sure everyone ascends about the same time...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is one possibility that I've heard about before. It also makes sense from a story telling point, as you shouldn't really be able to just buy fame (Legend) on a whim. It should be earned for your deeds of service / terror. So having the ST in charge of giving out Legend is better than spending XP on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T15:51:28-07:00","id":885745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/831580-must-a-scion-ascend?p=885421#post885421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That is one possibility that I've heard about before. It also makes sense from a story telling point, as you shouldn't really be able to just buy fame (Legend) on a whim. It should be earned for your deeds of service / terror. So having the ST in charge of giving out Legend is better than spending XP on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, if you do it that way, you need to rebalance awarding XP. Otherwise the characters will be massively overpowered at each and every dot of Legend. Even though the monsters are badly balanced as is, they and the Scion NPCs will also be complete cakewalks to your &quot;ST whim Legend allocations&quot; XP bloated PCs.<br /> <br /> Considering the amount of XP that is supposed to be sunk into Legend, probably cut out at least 1/4 at Hero and progressively more at Demigod and God. <br /> <br /> Cause and effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}